.Dd July 31, 2026
.Dt LIBSHMRING 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm shmring_create_with_options ,
.Nm shmring_create ,
.Nm shmring_open ,
.Nm shmring_write ,
.Nm shmring_read ,
.Nm shmring_write_record ,
.Nm shmring_read_record ,
.Nm shmring_readable ,
.Nm shmring_writable
.Nd capability-safe shared-memory transport rings
.Sh LIBRARY
.Li libshmring
.Pq Fl lshmring
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In shmring.h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
library creates bounded, unidirectional shared-memory rings for communication
between capability-mode processes.
The versioned
.Vt struct shmring_options
selects a small number of transport shapes, not arbitrary implementation
tuning.
.Dv SHMRING_SHAPE_COMPACT_SPSC
is a 4 through 64 KiB single-producer, single-consumer ring for ordinary
component traffic.
.Dv SHMRING_SHAPE_BULK_SPSC
is a 64 KiB through 1 GiB SPSC ring for sustained bulk traffic.
The 64 KiB boundary is valid for either shape so a typed library can state
its intended policy unambiguously.
.Dv SHMRING_SHAPE_TRUSTED_MPSC
is reserved for trusted internal shard workers and currently fails with
.Er ENOTSUP ;
it will not be enabled until a reservation/commit API can preserve records
when a producer stalls or dies.
.Pp
Applications should not select these shapes directly.
A typed client library should begin on its control channel, allocate a compact
ring only after sustained traffic, and promote to bulk only under pressure.
Idle sessions therefore consume no shared-memory ring.
.Pp
Supported rings are single-producer, single-consumer.
Callers with multiple producer or consumer threads must serialize access on
the corresponding side.
Each endpoint consists of separate immutable configuration, data,
producer-head, and consumer-tail descriptors.
Descriptor rights ensure that only the producer can modify data and the head,
and only the consumer can modify the tail.
.Pp
Opened ring mappings are marked
.Dv INHERIT_NONE
and are therefore unmapped in children created by
.Xr fork 2 .
Ring objects also record their creating process and reject use from a child
with
.Er ECHILD .
A child that needs a ring must receive and open a newly authorized endpoint.
.Pp
.Dv SHMRING_MODE_STREAM
provides a byte stream.
.Dv SHMRING_MODE_RECORD
preserves record boundaries and is suitable for datagrams and framed
component messages.
Capacities must be powers of two between
.Dv SHMRING_MIN_CAPACITY
and
.Dv SHMRING_MAX_CAPACITY .
Optional low and high watermarks are immutable policy hints carried with the
ring and must be ordered within its capacity.
They do not themselves perform notification or flow control.
.Pp
The library does not provide wakeups.
Users should send edge notifications over a kqueueable
.Xr libservice 3
channel after publishing data or freeing space.
.Pp
.Fn shmring_readable
and
.Fn shmring_writable
return the currently available byte count, or -1 on error.
In particular, an empty or full ring returns zero while corrupt shared
positions return -1 with
.Er EPROTO .
Callers must not store these results in an unsigned type before checking for
failure.
.Pp
The
.Ql shmring
DTrace provider exposes creation and mapping with shape and mode, plus read,
write, close, and invariant-violation probes.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cap_enter 2 ,
.Xr fork 2 ,
.Xr minherit 2 ,
.Xr mmap 2 ,
.Xr libservice 3
.Sh SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
All shared state is validated before use.
Object identity, exact role-specific capability rights, sizes, required memfd
seals, and immutable geometry are checked before mappings are dereferenced,
so aliased, over-authorized, short, mutable, or malformed objects fail with
.Er EPROTO
rather than generating a mapping fault.
A violated position or record invariant fails with
.Er EPROTO .
Callers should treat that error as a compromised peer and destroy the
component session.
